$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of methyl malonic acid (4.5 g, 37.5 mmol) and benzylalcohol
(2.1 g, 15 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was cooled to 0 °C and EDC
hydrochloride (5.75 g, 30 mmol) was added in small portions. The
resulting mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred for
30 min. The reaction mixture was washed with H2O (20 mL) and extracted
with aq. sat. NaHCO3 (4 × 12 mL). The combined aqueous phases were
acidified to pH 3 by adding aq. HCl (4%) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 ×
10 mL). The combined organic phases were dried over NaSO4, which was then
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Tthe crude material.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
