$DATUM To the crude material (2.05 g, 9.8 mmol) and 4-methoxythiophenol (2.80 g,
19.7 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (25 mL) at 0 °C was added EDC hydrochloride
(3.80 g, 19.7 mmol) in small portions and the resulting mixture was
stirred for 1 hour at room temperature. The reaction was washed with
water (20 mL), extracted with CH2Cl2 and the combined organic phases were
concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was purified by flash column
chromatography (n-hexane/EtOAc). Benzyl
3-((4-methoxyphenyl)thio)-2-methyl-3-oxopropanoate 1b as colorless oil.
δH (300 MHz, CDCl3): 7.43-7.37 (m, 5 H, ArH), 7.36-7.27 (m, 2 H, ArH),
7.01-6.92 (m, 2 H, ArH), 5.25 (s, 2 H, ArCH2), 3.86 (s, 3 H, OCH3),
3.85-3-76 (m, 1 H, CH), 1.55 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 3 H, CH3); δc (101 MHz,
CDCl3): 194.6 (C), 169.1 (C), 160.9 (C), 136.2 (CH), 135.4 (C), 128.6
(CH), 128.4 (CH), 128.2 (CH), 117.5 (C), 115.0 (CH), 67.3 (CH2), 55.4
(CH3), 53.5 (CH), 14.2 (CH3); HRMS (ESI): calculated for C18H19O4S [M+H]+
331.0999, found 331.0997; υmax(neat)/cm-1: 3033, 2940, 1738, 1696, 1591,
1573, 1493, 1376;
